@startuml UC24_ViewDoctorDashboard
' Sử dụng cấu trúc <style> mới thay cho skinparam cũ
<style>
document {
  ' Ép khoảng cách chiều dọc và ngang kịch sàn
  ParticipantPadding 5
  BoxPadding 5
}
</style>

' Bạn vẫn có thể giữ lại các lệnh skinparam về font và dpi dưới đây:
skinparam dpi 70
skinparam DefaultFontSize 10
skinparam SequenceMessageFontSize 9
'================================================================
' UC-24: View Doctor Dashboard
' Sequence Diagram – Detailed Design Level
' Primary Actor  : Doctor
' Classes : AppointmentController, AppointmentService (interface),
'           AppointmentServiceImpl, AppointmentRepository,
'           DoctorRepository, Appointment, AppointmentStatus,
'           AppointmentResponse, AppointmentDashboardResponse,
'           ApiResponse
'================================================================
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #DDEEFF
    BorderColor     #336699
    FontStyle       bold
}
skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor #FFFACD
    BorderColor     #CC9900
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FFFFF0
    BorderColor     #AAAAAA
}
skinparam ArrowColor #336699
skinparam LifeLineBorderColor #336699

title UC-24: View Doctor Dashboard\n(Detailed Design – Sequence Diagram)

'--- Participants (ordered left → right, mirroring class diagram) ---
actor "Doctor" as Actor
participant "<<Controller>>\nAppointmentController"        as AC
participant "<<Service>>\nAppointmentService\n(interface)" as AS
participant "<<ServiceImpl>>\nAppointmentServiceImpl"      as ASImpl
participant "<<Repository>>\nAppointmentRepository"        as ARepo
participant "<<Repository>>\nDoctorRepository"             as DRepo
entity      "<<Entity>>\nAppointment"                      as Appt
entity      "<<Entity>>\nAppointmentStatus"                as ApptStatus
participant "<<DTO>>\nAppointmentDashboardResponse"        as DashResp
participant "<<DTO>>\nAppointmentResponse"                 as ApptResp
participant "<<DTO>>\nApiResponse"                         as ApiResp

'================================================================
' PRE-CONDITION
'================================================================
note over Actor
  PRE-1: Doctor is authenticated (JWT role = DOCTOR).
  PRE-2: Doctor can only view their own dashboard and queue.
end note

'================================================================
' NORMAL FLOW – Step 1 & 2: Doctor navigates; System defaults to today
'================================================================
== Step 1 & 2 – Navigate to Dashboard (Default: today) ==

Actor -> AC : GET /api/v1/appointments/dashboard\n[?date=<optional>]\n[Authorization: Bearer <JWT>]
activate AC
note right of AC
  Spring Security resolves actor role from JWT.
  resolveDoctorId(userDetails) maps email → Doctor.id
end note

AC -> DRepo : findByEmail(userDetails.getUsername())
activate DRepo
DRepo --> AC : Optional<Doctor>
deactivate DRepo

AC -> AC : resolveDoctorId(userDetails)\n→ doctorId (Long)

AC -> AS : getDashboard(date, doctorId)
activate AS
AS -> ASImpl : getDashboard(date, doctorId)
activate ASImpl

ASImpl -> ASImpl : targetDate = (date != null) ? date : LocalDate.now()\nstart = targetDate.atStartOfDay()\nend   = targetDate.plusDays(1).atStartOfDay()

ASImpl -> ARepo : countByDateAndDoctorId(start, end, doctorId)
activate ARepo
ARepo --> ASImpl : long total
deactivate ARepo

loop for each AppointmentStatus s in\n[PENDING, CONFIRMED, WAITING, IN_PROGRESS, COMPLETED, CANCELLED]
    ASImpl -> ARepo : countByDateAndStatusAndDoctorId(start, end, s, doctorId)
    activate ARepo
    ARepo --> ASImpl : long count
    deactivate ARepo
end

ASImpl -> DashResp : AppointmentDashboardResponse.builder()\n  .total(total).pending(…).confirmed(…)\n  .waiting(…).inProgress(…)\n  .completed(…).cancelled(…).build()
activate DashResp
DashResp --> ASImpl : AppointmentDashboardResponse
deactivate DashResp

ASImpl --> AS   : AppointmentDashboardResponse
deactivate ASImpl
AS     --> AC   : AppointmentDashboardResponse
deactivate AS

AC -> ApiResp : success(AppointmentDashboardResponse)
activate ApiResp
ApiResp --> AC : ApiResponse<AppointmentDashboardResponse>{status=200, data=…}
deactivate ApiResp

AC --> Actor : HTTP 200 OK\n{ total, pending, confirmed,\n  waiting, inProgress, completed, cancelled }
deactivate AC

'================================================================
' NORMAL FLOW – Step 3: Display appointments grouped by time slot
'================================================================
== Step 3 – Load Doctor Queue ==

Actor -> AC : GET /api/v1/appointments/doctor-queue\n[?date=<optional>]\n[Authorization: Bearer <JWT>]
activate AC

AC -> DRepo : findByEmail(userDetails.getUsername())
activate DRepo
DRepo --> AC : Optional<Doctor>
deactivate DRepo

AC -> AC : resolveDoctorId(userDetails) → doctorId

AC -> AS : getDoctorQueue(date, doctorId)
activate AS
AS -> ASImpl : getDoctorQueue(date, doctorId)
activate ASImpl

ASImpl -> ASImpl : targetDate / start / end computed

ASImpl -> ARepo : findByAppointmentDateAndDoctorIdOrderByAppointmentTimeAsc\n(start, end, doctorId)
activate ARepo
note right of ARepo
  JPQL:
  SELECT a FROM Appointment a
  WHERE appointmentTime >= :start
    AND appointmentTime  < :end
    AND doctor.id = :doctorId
    AND status IN ('WAITING','IN_PROGRESS',
                   'COMPLETED','CONFIRMED')
  ORDER BY appointmentTime ASC
end note
ARepo -> Appt : SELECT … (filtered by doctorId)
activate Appt
Appt --> ARepo : List<Appointment>
deactivate Appt
ARepo --> ASImpl : List<Appointment>
deactivate ARepo

loop for each Appointment a in list
    ASImpl -> ApptStatus : a.getStatus()
    activate ApptStatus
    ApptStatus --> ASImpl : AppointmentStatus
    deactivate ApptStatus

    ASImpl -> ApptResp : AppointmentResponse.builder()\n  .id / .patientId / .patientName / .patientPhone\n  .doctorId / .doctorName / .serviceName\n  .appointmentTime / .timeSlot / .status\n  .type / .queueNumber / .checkInTime\n  .notes / .createdAt … .build()
    activate ApptResp
    ApptResp --> ASImpl : AppointmentResponse
    deactivate ApptResp
end

ASImpl --> AS   : List<AppointmentResponse>
deactivate ASImpl
AS     --> AC   : List<AppointmentResponse>
deactivate AS

AC -> ApiResp : success(List<AppointmentResponse>)
activate ApiResp
ApiResp --> AC : ApiResponse<List<AppointmentResponse>>{status=200, data=[…]}
deactivate ApiResp

AC --> Actor : HTTP 200 OK\n{ list of appointments grouped by timeSlot:\n  patientName, statusBadge, doctorName }
deactivate AC

note over Actor
  Step 3 – UI renders cards per time slot:
  – patient name, status badge (color-coded), doctor name
  – Doctor view: own queue only (sorted by appointmentTime ASC)
end note

'================================================================
' NORMAL FLOW – Step 4: Filter / Search
'================================================================
== Step 4 – Doctor Searches by Patient Name ==

Actor -> AC : GET /api/v1/appointments/search?keyword={patientName}\n[Authorization: Bearer <JWT>]
activate AC

AC -> AS : searchAppointments(keyword)
activate AS
AS -> ASImpl : searchAppointments(keyword)
activate ASImpl

alt keyword is null or blank
    ASImpl -> ARepo : findAllWithDetails()
    activate ARepo
    note right of ARepo
      JPQL:
      SELECT DISTINCT a FROM Appointment a
      LEFT JOIN FETCH a.patient
      LEFT JOIN FETCH a.doctor
      LEFT JOIN FETCH a.clinicService
      ORDER BY appointmentTime DESC
    end note
    ARepo -> Appt : SELECT * (all records)
    activate Appt
    Appt --> ARepo : List<Appointment>
    deactivate Appt
    ARepo --> ASImpl : List<Appointment>
    deactivate ARepo
else keyword NOT blank
    ASImpl -> ARepo : searchAppointments(keyword.trim())
    activate ARepo
    note right of ARepo
      JPQL:
      WHERE LOWER(patient.fullName) LIKE '%keyword%'
         OR patient.phone           LIKE '%keyword%'
         OR CAST(patient.id AS str) LIKE '%keyword%'
      ORDER BY appointmentTime DESC, timeSlot ASC
    end note
    ARepo -> Appt : SELECT … (filtered by keyword)
    activate Appt
    Appt --> ARepo : List<Appointment>
    deactivate Appt
    ARepo --> ASImpl : List<Appointment>
    deactivate ARepo
end

loop for each Appointment a in results
    ASImpl -> ApptResp : AppointmentResponse.builder() … .build()
    activate ApptResp
    ApptResp --> ASImpl : AppointmentResponse
    deactivate ApptResp
end

ASImpl --> AS   : List<AppointmentResponse>
deactivate ASImpl
AS     --> AC   : List<AppointmentResponse>
deactivate AS

AC -> ApiResp : success(List<AppointmentResponse>)
activate ApiResp
ApiResp --> AC : ApiResponse<List<AppointmentResponse>>{status=200, data=[…]}
deactivate ApiResp

AC --> Actor : HTTP 200 OK { searched appointment list }
deactivate AC

'================================================================
' NORMAL FLOW – Step 5: Actor clicks an appointment card (detail)
'================================================================
== Step 5 – Doctor Clicks a Card to View Appointment Detail (Read-Only) ==

Actor -> AC : GET /api/v1/appointments/{id}\n[Authorization: Bearer <JWT>]
activate AC

AC -> AS : getAppointmentById(id)
activate AS
AS -> ASImpl : getAppointmentById(id)
activate ASImpl

ASImpl -> ARepo : findById(id)
activate ARepo
ARepo -> Appt : SELECT * WHERE id = ?
activate Appt
Appt --> ARepo : Optional<Appointment>
deactivate Appt
ARepo --> ASImpl : Appointment
deactivate ARepo

ASImpl -> ApptStatus : a.getStatus()
activate ApptStatus
ApptStatus --> ASImpl : AppointmentStatus
deactivate ApptStatus

ASImpl -> ApptResp : AppointmentResponse.builder()\n  .id / .patientId / .patientName / .patientPhone\n  .doctorId / .doctorName / .serviceName\n  .appointmentTime / .timeSlot / .status\n  .type / .queueNumber / .checkInTime\n  .notes / .createdAt … .build()
activate ApptResp
ApptResp --> ASImpl : AppointmentResponse (full detail)
deactivate ApptResp

ASImpl --> AS   : AppointmentResponse
deactivate ASImpl
AS     --> AC   : AppointmentResponse
deactivate AS

AC -> ApiResp : success(AppointmentResponse)
activate ApiResp
ApiResp --> AC : ApiResponse<AppointmentResponse>{status=200, data=…}
deactivate ApiResp

AC --> Actor : HTTP 200 OK { full appointment detail:\n  patientName, phone, doctor, service,\n  timeSlot, status, queueNumber, notes }
deactivate AC

note over Actor
  Step 5 – UI renders read-only detail panel:
  – Doctor: read-only view of patient info & appointment detail.
end note

'================================================================
' ALTERNATIVE FLOW – ALT-1: View another date
'================================================================
== ALT-1 – Doctor Selects a Different Date from the Calendar Widget ==

Actor -> AC : GET /api/v1/appointments/dashboard?date={selectedDate}\n[Authorization: Bearer <JWT>]
activate AC
note right of AC
  ALT-1: Doctor picks a date ≠ today via calendar widget.
  System passes ?date=YYYY-MM-DD as a @RequestParam.
  The rest of the flow is identical to Normal Flow Step 2
  with targetDate = selectedDate instead of LocalDate.now().
end note

AC -> AS : getDashboard(selectedDate, doctorId)
activate AS
AS -> ASImpl : getDashboard(selectedDate, doctorId)
activate ASImpl

ASImpl -> ASImpl : targetDate = selectedDate\nstart = targetDate.atStartOfDay()\nend   = targetDate.plusDays(1).atStartOfDay()

ASImpl -> ARepo : countByDateAndDoctorId(start, end, doctorId)
activate ARepo
ARepo --> ASImpl : counts per status
deactivate ARepo

ASImpl -> DashResp : AppointmentDashboardResponse.builder() … .build()
activate DashResp
DashResp --> ASImpl : AppointmentDashboardResponse (for selectedDate)
deactivate DashResp

ASImpl --> AS   : AppointmentDashboardResponse
deactivate ASImpl
AS     --> AC   : AppointmentDashboardResponse
deactivate AS

AC -> ApiResp : success(AppointmentDashboardResponse)
activate ApiResp
ApiResp --> AC : ApiResponse<AppointmentDashboardResponse>{status=200}
deactivate ApiResp

AC --> Actor : HTTP 200 OK { schedule reloaded for selectedDate }
deactivate AC

note over Actor
  UI re-renders the dashboard for the selected date.
  POST-1: Schedule is displayed with real-time status counts.
end note

'================================================================
' POST-CONDITIONS
'================================================================
note over Actor
  POST-1: Schedule is displayed with real-time status.
  No data mutation occurs in this use case.
end note
@enduml
